_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "154920"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "155047"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "155177"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "259031"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "308111"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "356962"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "19001705"} "2020"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/248"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Cross-Country, Women" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "28 July 2024 — 14:10"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2177"} "Élancourt Hill, Saint-Quentin-en-Yvelines, France"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/2003676"} "36 from 28 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "30.8 km"]] [:tr {} [:th {:valign "top"} "Details"] [:td {} "Distance: 30.8 km" [:br {}] "Intermediate 1: 4.4 km" [:br {}] "Intermediate 2: 8.8 km" [:br {}] "Intermediate 3: 13.2 km" [:br {}] "Intermediate 4: 17.6 km" [:br {}] "Intermediate 5: 22 km" [:br {}] "Intermediate 6: 26.4 km"]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Switzerland had completed a podium sweep in Tokyo, but only " [:a {:href "/athletes/146640"} "Sina Frei"] " made the start list in Paris. Her compatriot " [:a {:href "/athletes/131734"} "Jolanda Neff"] ", who had won gold at the Tokyo Games, did not defend her Olympic title in Paris after withdrawing due to illness. The defending World Champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/125024"} "Pauline Ferrand-Prévot"] " (FRA) was in Paris looking to win Olympic gold, along with the other medalists at the recent World Championships, " [:a {:href "/athletes/142729"} "Loana Lecomte"] " (FRA) and " [:a {:href "/athletes/151607"} "Puck Pieterse"] " (NED). Other favorites included " [:a {:href "/athletes/2505215"} "Blanka Vas"] " (HUN), " [:a {:href "/athletes/131138"} "Anne Terpstra"] " (NED), " [:a {:href "/athletes/142989"} "Evie Richards"] " (GBR), " [:a {:href "/athletes/2504481"} "Laura Stigger"] " (AUT), and the 2016 Rio de Janeiro gold medalist " [:a {:href "/athletes/131772"} "Jenny Rissveds"] " (SWE)."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Following the mass start, a breakaway group containing Ferrand-Prévot, Pieterse, Stigger, and Lecomte had a 10-second lead over the rest of the field by the end of the first lap. Lecomte suffered a bad crash on descending the rock section on the third lap and was unable to finish the race. Ferrand-Prévot dominated the rest of the race, never losing her lead over the rest of the field, eventually finishing almost three minutes ahead of her nearest rival to win gold. " [:a {:href "/athletes/147168"} "Haley Batten"] " (USA) was the surprise of the race after she just pipped Jenny Rissveds to win silver, with Puck Pieterse finishing fourth."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Bib"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {} "Lap 1"] [:th {} "Lap 2"] [:th {} "Lap 3"] [:th {} "Lap 4"] [:th {} "Lap 5"] [:th {} "Lap 6"] [:th {} "Lap 7"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/125024"} "Pauline Ferrand-Prévot"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRA.png"}] "FRA"]] [:td {} "1-26:02"] [:td {} "12:21 (1)"] [:td {} "11:45 (1)"] [:td {} "12:09 (1)"] [:td {} "12:14 (1)"] [:td {} "12:18 (1)"] [:td {} "12:31 (1)"] [:td {} "12:44 (5)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] 